id           = CWE-673
name         = External Influence of Sphere Definition
abstraction  = Class
structure    = Simple
status       = Draft

description : The product does not prevent the definition of control spheres from external actors.

extended description : Typically, a product defines its control sphere within the code itself, or through configuration by the product's administrator. In some cases, an external party can change the definition of the control sphere. This is typically a resultant weakness.

notes : https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/673.html
